WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Take 2 protons and 2 neutrons,
and weigh them one by one.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.860
Now let the same four particles
bind together into a helium nucleus,

3
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.180
and weigh that.

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.750
The balance tips.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.300
The nucleus comes out lighter
than the parts it is made from.

6
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.260
Not one proton or neutron is missing.

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.610
So where did the missing mass go?

8
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.400
In this mission, you'll weigh
atoms in a unit built for them:

9
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.060
one twelfth of a carbon-12 atom.

10
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.410
Then you'll compare the masses on
both sides of a fusion reaction,

11
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.420
where a deuterium nucleus
and a tritium nucleus fuse.

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: find out
where the missing mass went.
